/-!
# Endpoint atom to a source-generated high-frequency PDE responsibility

The endpoint full-pair write already identifies a positive kinetic atom with
a nonsettling whole physical residual tail.  The bounded old run independently
generates arbitrarily large high-frequency aggregate responsibilities.

This module makes those two facts one same-source statement: the atom itself
sets the aggregate mass quantum.  At every requested radius the old run
therefore generates a larger finite core, a nonzero native gluing redirect,
or a finite aggregate whose coefficient mass is strictly larger than half
the atom and whose physical rate obstruction is paid on the same actual
restart event.

The caller supplies only the actual endpoint lineage and stage.  The atom,
mass quantum, radius response, crossing, output family, gluing branch,
positive time, and physical rate alternative are generated internally.
-/

